    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogy. Let's focus on the physics.\n\nThe pressure difference is created because of the shape of the wing. As air flows over the curved surface of the wing, it must travel faster to follow the curve. This is because the air molecules are being forced to change direction, which increases their velocity. According to Bernoulli's principle, if the velocity of a fluid (like air) increases, its pressure decreases.\n\nSo, when air flows over the top of the wing, it accelerates and its pressure decreases. This creates a region of lower pressure above the wing. At the same time, the air flowing along the flat bottom surface of the wing is moving more slowly, which increases its pressure. This creates a region of higher pressure below the wing.\n\nThe pressure difference between the top and bottom surfaces of the wing creates an upward force, or lift, that counteracts the weight of the aircraft. The faster-moving air on top of the wing creates a region of lower pressure, which pulls the wing upward, while the slower-moving air on the bottom creates a region of higher pressure, which pushes the wing downward. The difference in pressure between these two regions creates the lift force that allows the aircraft",
